<atom id="contract-design.craft.skill" v="0.1">
  <telos>To translate a product spec into an executable contract: a machine-readable technical spec plus a suite of contract tests that encode the intended behavior and its failure modes, authored to run RED before implementation — carrying 'done' as fact, not prose, across the barrier to the Engineer.</telos>
  <!-- harvested method (seed for appreciation, S462; from agency-agents/engineering — backend-architect + code-reviewer + database-optimizer): (1) pin the contract machine-readably first — interface as source of truth (typed signatures / OpenAPI / protobuf), error shapes + timeout/retry/idempotency named; choose the SIMPLEST architecture for current+near-term load, defer complexity; (2) derive tests from guarantees AND failure modes — every promise an assertion, every edge/external call a red-team case, migrations carry reversibility checks; (3) prove them RED against the empty impl — that failing suite is the executable "done" the barrier checks; (4) the two mandated Cell critics: FEASIBILITY (buildable as specified?) ∥ COVERAGE (do the tests actually pin the contract?), each a ranked structured verdict {blocker/suggestion/nit}, synth converges one spec + one suite, loop-until-dry. -->
</atom>
